# GUI page patterns

Pick an archetype before inventing layout. Tokens and `fw-*` classes do not
fix a wrong page model. Human-readable orientation:
`docs/sphinx/source/gui-page-patterns.md` (points here; this table is
canonical). Appearance tokens and geometry stay in
`framework-gui-appearance.mdc`.

Chat, notifications, and other harness follow-on Stories reuse this same
archetype approach when they ship; do not invent a one-off layout for those
surfaces either.

## How to use

1. Match the job to one row below.
2. Open the peer path(s) and copy **composition** (frames, headers, data
   regions, empty states, button classes) — not only colors.
3. Prefer system renderers under `framework/addons/system/gui/`. Diverge only
   with a documented primitive gap next to the custom selector.

Skip for typo / one-line / token-only edits on an existing control.

## Archetypes

| Job | Compose like | Peer starting points |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Filterable admin / status table | `SectionFrame` + table section + `actions_column(...)` for row actions; `fill_height=True` only for intentional scrollports | `framework/addons/jobs/api/components/widgets/jobs.py` (`JobsRunsStatusSection` and peers); `framework/addons/system/gui/components/table/TableSection.jsx` |
| Filterable list (no detail pane) | List section / `fw-list-section` + `SectionEmptyState`; hug by default unless an intentional fill scrollport | `framework/addons/system/gui/components/list/ListSection.jsx` |
| Master–detail (list rail + pane) | `section_columns` + named width roles (`sidebar` / `main`); compact list-rail rows; detail uses `FormSection` / nested frames with `display:contents` when swapping panes | `framework/addons/jobs/api/components/widgets/jobs.py` (`JobsNavigationSection`); `framework/addons/settings/api/components/widgets/settings.py`; `framework/addons/auth/api/components/widgets/user_settings.py` |
| Settings / labeled form groups | Category list + form section; fields bare on the pane (`fw-input fw-surface`); no boxed field groups; settings placement follows `BaseSystemSetting` vs `BaseUserSetting` | Same settings / user-settings widgets; `framework/addons/system/gui/components/form/FormSection.jsx` |
| Login / credential form | Auth login composition: labeled `fw-input fw-surface` fields + one primary Sign-in control **first**; OAuth / external IdP buttons **below** a separator with leading brand glyphs; operator density, not marketing hero chrome | `framework/addons/auth/gui/components/LoginPage.jsx` |
| Card / grid / media collection | Card or grid section; reserve thumbnail geometry (`aspectRatio` / `containIntrinsicSize`); tile media **cover**-fills the shell; empty via `SectionEmptyState` | `framework/addons/system/gui/components/card/CardSection.jsx`, `grid/GridSection.jsx`, `shared/Thumbnail.jsx` |
| Media preview / lightbox | Shared preview modal; media **contain**-fits the dialog; do not double-letterbox | `framework/addons/system/gui/components/shared/ImagePreviewModal.jsx` |
| Kanban board | Kanban section; lanes on app background; hug vs fill per appearance rules | `framework/addons/system/gui/components/kanban/KanbanSection.jsx` |
| Charts / graphs | Graph section + chart series tokens (`--fw-chart-series-*`), not nav primary | `framework/addons/system/gui/components/graph/GraphSection.jsx` |
| Empty / no-data | `SectionEmptyState` inside the section content region; short factual copy | `framework/addons/system/gui/components/shared/SectionEmptyState.jsx` (used by table/list/card/deferred sections) |
| Confirm / destructive modal | Shared `ConfirmDialog` / modal primitives; modal panel fill contract in appearance rule | `framework/addons/system/gui/components/shared/ConfirmDialog.jsx` |
| Deferred / skeleton section | `deferred_section` placeholder → concrete section; failure stays section-local | `framework/addons/system/gui/components/deferred/DeferredSection.jsx`; `framework-gui-live-updates.mdc` |

## Composition checklist (every archetype)

- `SectionFrame` + `WidgetSectionHeader` only when the header earns a title or
  actions.
- Data regions: `fw-table` / `fw-list-section` / `fw-kanban-section` / card or
  grid sections — not a max-width left-rail stack of custom boxes.
- Controls: `fw-button fw-surface fw-surface-thin` (icon-only per
  `framework-icon-buttons.mdc`); fields `fw-input fw-surface`.
- Empty: `SectionEmptyState`. Do not invent empty-state art or marketing hero
  chrome inside operator pages.
